{"title":"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the integer closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407d0bdc94cf0863b010582ed22b48dbeb69d16a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[4]{n}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a119a7bc233a7e57e170c14b1b783a338ba70363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{1995}\\frac 1{f(k)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"75\" height=\"56\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1bde402c415b30d44db3288ca6e97613157d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(k - \\frac {1}{2}\\right)^4 \\leq n &lt; \\left(k + \\frac {1}{2}\\right)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"216\" height=\"46\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1b2264d810643278c486d0427cd2078fbf3133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />. Thus there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7bee35e382a796e4f5c9733b082ba84eb45995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor \\left(k + \\frac {1}{2}\\right)^4 - \\left(k - \\frac {1}{2}\\right)^4 \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"198\" height=\"53\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1b2264d810643278c486d0427cd2078fbf3133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />. Expanding using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Binomial theorem\">binomial theorem</a>, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48cdd58ad7608353239ce78453da6d3ac9e8647.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left(k + \\frac {1}{2}\\right)^4 - \\left(k - \\frac {1}{2}\\right)^4 &amp;= \\left(k^4 + 2k^3 + \\frac 32k^2 + \\frac 12k + \\frac 1{16}\\right) - \\left(k^4 - 2k^3 + \\frac 32k^2 - \\frac 12k + \\frac 1{16}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= 4k^3 + k. \\end{align*}\" width=\"689\" height=\"69\" /> \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23b1f515e897f6d31064cbef10dd4652c328b993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" /> appears in the summation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3df7c8ec8cfbf34b21b77b7eab5643258bfa4f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k^3 + k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> times, and the sum for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/7/a278b3a7708d57c508833cc9a54f9b220a4611bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4k^3 + k) \\cdot \\frac{1}{k} = 4k^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"184\" height=\"38\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/5030b8b2e1983047683733deb951a552b42ed896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/06973c3dca4a219c71e607723ce8bd2bab24d149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{6} 4k^2 + 1 = 364 + 6 = 370$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"220\" height=\"50\" /> (either adding or using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">sum of consecutive squares formula</a>).  \n</p><p>But this only accounts for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7017800a307a1e901762458077977f2e063cadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k = 1}^{6} (4k^3 + k) = 4\\left(\\frac{6(6+1)}{2}\\right)^2 + \\frac{6(6+1)}{2} = 1764 + 21 = 1785$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"487\" height=\"50\" /> terms, so we still have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a47700fb47f15e528ecf423c2fbde5cbd5d34d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1995 - 1785$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b4328d77715c539955c57ce1aee7b7bc9cdea458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> terms with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a51b9b2af524a6a626d9ea5bb580e4c759ab79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />. This adds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374c71eefe9af8cefcc7ac0ea168aa0f6b490087.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210 \\cdot \\frac {1}{7} = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" /> to our summation, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd10d22c2428d464d0d13654fcd957f20a63c9db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is a pretty easy problem just to bash. Since the max number we can get is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we just need to test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20acbc58522b2c1662bb955d27b9eff944db4bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5,2.5,3.5,4.5,5.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7314f8133d3b925b9ce6598191d153da7ecdd779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. Then just do how many numbers there are times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb50636d4e633c1b6c0542069dd5d8895ed5c50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\lfloor n \\rfloor}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"29\" height=\"42\" />, which should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e416c59c8e1c63a61503db0652ff4dead8de718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+17+37+65+101+145+30 = \\boxed{400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"333\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME\" title=\"1995 AIME\">1995 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185016\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 223/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1770/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 92/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5700/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.845      1 -total\n 58.68%    7.538      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.95%    5.003      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2965:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185016 and revision id 292191. Rendering was triggered beca